00:15:17.549 --> 00:15:19.118
A full century after

00:15:19.118 --> 00:15:20.152 align:start size:88% position:13%
the end of World War II.
- [Dave] Right.

00:15:20.152 --> 00:15:21.887 align:start size:84% position:16%
Right.
- Okay, so we gotta,

00:15:21.887 --> 00:15:23.856
we gotta basically a 10,

00:15:23.856 --> 00:15:26.692
10 year timeline to
really do it right.

00:15:28.027 --> 00:15:32.498 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that involves significant
non-clinical research,

00:15:32.498 --> 00:15:35.868 align:start size:97% position:3%
toxicology, pharmaco
distribution, genotoxicity,

00:15:35.868 --> 00:15:40.873
a whole bunch of things
that just got blown off

00:15:41.607 --> 00:15:43.075
to make sure that,

00:15:43.075 --> 00:15:46.512 align:start position:0%
that it's safe enough to go
into humans in the first place.

00:15:46.512 --> 00:15:48.914
And then once it's
in humans, it go,

00:15:48.914 --> 00:15:52.851 align:start size:97% position:3%
typically a vaccine goes
through a very staged process

00:15:52.851 --> 00:15:54.453
of phase one trials,

00:15:54.453 --> 00:15:57.389 align:start size:97% position:3%
typically a couple of
different phase one trials,

00:15:57.389 --> 00:16:00.359
phase two expanded trials.

00:16:00.359 --> 00:16:03.762
Phase one is typically just
kind of preliminary estimates

00:16:03.762 --> 00:16:06.465
of safety with low numbers.

00:16:06.465 --> 00:16:09.301 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, here's an
important thing to know.

00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:11.704
In vaccinology we use
the rule of three.

00:16:13.105 --> 00:16:16.175
And the way this works
is if you wanna detect

00:16:16.175 --> 00:16:19.845
an adverse event that occurs
in one in a thousand people,

00:16:21.013 --> 00:16:24.283
generally you have
to test 3000 people.

00:16:25.751 --> 00:16:30.356
If you wanna detect something
that happens one in 30, okay.

00:16:31.557 --> 00:16:32.925
Or one in 10, I was
gonna say one in 10,

00:16:32.925 --> 00:16:34.593
then you'd have to
test 30 people, okay.

00:16:34.593 --> 00:16:36.595
So that's kind of
phase one trial.

00:16:36.595 --> 00:16:37.429
- [Dave] Right.

00:16:37.429 --> 00:16:38.664
Level one in, you know,

00:16:38.664 --> 00:16:41.400
one in 10 is stuff
that happens a lot,

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:43.135
pretty much to everybody, right?

00:16:44.069 --> 00:16:46.238
One of the thousand is,

00:16:46.238 --> 00:16:48.907
is something that matters
a lot if you're gonna be

00:16:48.907 --> 00:16:51.110
administering it to
large populations.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.712 align:start size:84% position:16%
Which generally is the
case with vaccines,

00:16:53.712 --> 00:16:55.647
unless you're talking
about special forces

00:16:55.647 --> 00:16:58.450 align:start size:84% position:16%
or something for some
obscure pathogen.

00:16:59.718 --> 00:17:01.987 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then when you
really get to, you know,

00:17:03.188 --> 00:17:05.724
global deployment or
national deployment,

00:17:05.724 --> 00:17:10.729
you want to have sample sizes
in the kind of 300,000 range.

00:17:12.598 --> 00:17:14.033
You know, the,

00:17:14.033 --> 00:17:15.901 align:start size:97% position:3%
this is what the FDA has
typically required in the past

00:17:15.901 --> 00:17:20.906
for new adjuvants, for
example, for a vaccine.

00:17:21.807 --> 00:17:23.342
But in this case,

00:17:23.342 --> 00:17:27.246
kind of all the rules went
out the door in the rush,

00:17:27.246 --> 00:17:30.716
in all the fear that
was actively promoted.

00:17:32.951 --> 00:17:36.488
So when you, when you do
it that step-wise fashion,

00:17:36.488 --> 00:17:38.724
and then typically
what happens is you,

00:17:38.724 --> 00:17:43.729 align:start size:84% position:16%
you first kind of
move it forward in
healthy normal adults.

00:17:45.064 --> 00:17:48.300 align:start position:0%
Because they have lowest
risks, they can handle insults,

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:50.402
biologic insults best.

00:17:50.402 --> 00:17:51.837
And then,

00:17:51.837 --> 00:17:56.475 align:start size:97% position:3%
then you move to elderly
people and special populations

00:17:57.876 --> 00:17:59.945
like immunosuppressed and
those kinds of things.

00:17:59.945 --> 00:18:04.183
And you do a step down into
the little babies, okay?

00:18:04.183 --> 00:18:06.618 align:start size:97% position:3%
So first you do adolescents
and then you do,

00:18:06.618 --> 00:18:09.254 align:start size:97% position:3%
at first you do young adults,
then you do adolescents,

00:18:09.254 --> 00:18:13.258
then you do children, then
you do, you know, young,

00:18:13.258 --> 00:18:15.027 align:start size:84% position:16%
very young, and
then you can go down

00:18:15.027 --> 00:18:17.529
to neonates if you have to.

00:18:17.529 --> 00:18:19.298
So that's the general process.

00:18:19.298 --> 00:18:21.967
And to do all that takes
enormous amount of time.

00:18:21.967 --> 00:18:26.972
And the cost per subject for
a well-run trial is something,

00:18:28.507 --> 00:18:31.009
it starts at about
10,000 per person.

00:18:31.009 --> 00:18:34.213
Generally if you, if you
really mind your nickels,

00:18:34.213 --> 00:18:37.282 align:start size:97% position:3%
you can get it down to about
five or 8,000 per person,

00:18:37.282 --> 00:18:40.986
and it goes up to about
30 or 40,000 per person.

00:18:40.986 --> 00:18:44.523
So you can do the math and
you quickly come up to some

00:18:44.523 --> 00:18:46.792
serious, serious cash.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.695
So it, it takes, you know,

00:18:49.695 --> 00:18:54.700
billions of dollars, years
and years to do this safely.

00:18:55.868 --> 00:18:57.970
And as you've seen,

00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:00.873
the decision was to
rush the whole thing,

00:19:01.773 --> 00:19:04.243
bypass almost everything

00:19:06.612 --> 00:19:09.715
and start administering it into

00:19:09.715 --> 00:19:14.720 align:start size:88% position:13%
a very broad population,
a global population.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.289
And do so.

00:19:17.289 --> 00:19:20.459
Also bypassing this
key thing that was,

00:19:20.459 --> 00:19:24.263
we all agreed on in the
western world, at least.

00:19:24.263 --> 00:19:28.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
After World War II called
the Nuremberg Accords

00:19:28.367 --> 00:19:30.869
and the Helsinki Accords.

00:19:30.869 --> 00:19:34.840 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then in, in
moving to the present,

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:37.042
we call this the common rule.

00:19:37.042 --> 00:19:41.079
In which people have to be
granted informed consent.

00:19:41.079 --> 00:19:46.084
And you absolutely cannot
coerce, compel, or entice

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:50.889 align:start size:97% position:3%
people to take an
unlicensed medical product.

00:19:50.889 --> 00:19:54.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
That has just historically
been off limits.

00:19:54.293 --> 00:19:57.162 align:start size:84% position:16%
We all agreed, nope,
Germans did that.

00:19:57.162 --> 00:19:59.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, everybody
thinks about what happened

00:19:59.031 --> 00:20:00.132
in Nazi Germany.

00:20:01.567 --> 00:20:04.736
The story of what happened
in Japan is even uglier.

00:20:06.271 --> 00:20:10.342
The Japanese bio warfare
program was, you know,

00:20:10.342 --> 00:20:14.146 align:start size:88% position:13%
truly atrocious in
terms of the bioethics.

00:20:14.146 --> 00:20:18.917
And as I guess Bobby is gonna
point out in his next book.

00:20:19.918 --> 00:20:21.420
- Bobby Kennedy.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:25.290
- Just like we imported a lot
of the rocket scientists to

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.426
launch NASA, so to speak,

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:30.629
we imported both German,

00:20:30.629 --> 00:20:35.000 align:start size:97% position:3%
but particularly the
Japanese bio warfare experts

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:39.972
and the records associated
with that up to Fort Dietrich

00:20:41.373 --> 00:20:45.244 align:start position:0%
in Frederick, Maryland to
launch our bio warfare program.

00:20:46.411 --> 00:20:49.314 align:start size:84% position:16%
which after Nixon
made the determination

00:20:49.314 --> 00:20:51.550
that we were gonna put in place,

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:56.521 align:start size:84% position:16%
the bio warfare
treaty got transformed

00:20:57.422 --> 00:20:58.957
into a bio-defense program.

00:20:58.957 --> 00:21:01.760
The same people doing the
same stuff pretty much.

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:04.263
And that's, that's kind
of where that's all gone.

00:21:04.263 --> 00:21:06.131
It's, it's not a pretty picture.

00:21:07.299 --> 00:21:09.401
And, and the deeper
you look into it,

00:21:09.401 --> 00:21:12.738
and the bio labs that
we set up in Georgia,

00:21:12.738 --> 00:21:14.539
the former Soviet state,

00:21:14.539 --> 00:21:17.776 align:start position:0%
and then presumably the bio
labs that we set up in Ukraine,

00:21:19.611 --> 00:21:23.215
those, those offshore bio labs

00:21:24.616 --> 00:21:28.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
have a long, rich history
of ethical abuses,

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.522
let's say gently.

00:21:33.859 --> 00:21:36.228
So it's a mixed bag here.

00:21:36.228 --> 00:21:39.064
There's a lot of,
there's, there's.

00:21:39.064 --> 00:21:41.967 align:start size:84% position:16%
I do believe that
there is an unmet need

00:21:43.769 --> 00:21:47.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that was the logic
for advancing the RNA tech

00:21:47.673 --> 00:21:51.610 align:start size:97% position:3%
in theory was there
absolutely is an unmet need

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:54.413
for ability to respond rapidly

00:21:54.413 --> 00:21:58.317
to engineered pathogens and
emerging infectious disease.

00:22:02.354 --> 00:22:05.957
But I think personally
that what's been done

00:22:05.957 --> 00:22:10.962
will basically destroy global
public confidence in any of

00:22:12.397 --> 00:22:15.534
this kind of activity for
the foreseeable future.

00:22:15.534 --> 00:22:16.935
- Yeah, I think,

00:22:16.935 --> 00:22:19.638 align:start position:0%
I think we've done that already
and God only knows where

00:22:19.638 --> 00:22:21.873
that leads us when, when
something really big hits.

00:22:21.873 --> 00:22:23.308 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I, so I wanna
back up for a second.

00:22:23.308 --> 00:22:26.411 align:start position:0%
So when you got that call
around the second or fourth of,

00:22:26.411 --> 00:22:28.580
of January,

00:22:28.580 --> 00:22:30.015
back in 2020

00:22:30.015 --> 00:22:33.919 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now warp speed was basically
